{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11021-demonic-form-ideas","id":11021,"title":"Demonic Form Ideas!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T20:24:31-08:00","id":11021,"title":"Demonic Form Ideas!","content":"Come up with some cool ones yet? Description and/or Statistics, both are welcome! I'll start off:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Demonic Ophanim</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Wheels are well known to have the most unusual demonic forms amongst the Unchained, and those frequently identified with the Ophanim exemplify this. These strange beings take the form of four thick metallic wheels which whirl about the central body like a gyroscope, covered in eyes with pupils filled with static that wheep an oily substance that evaporates before it touches the ground. At the center of these rings sits a sphere covered in circuitry which makes the rough shape of a single watching eye. Electricity coruscates between the rings and the central sphere. Its central eye blinks with a hiss of steam released by the pressure of an eyelid made of wires, these strange beings are hot to the touch. From nodules on its center mass, floating metal manipulators emerge, allowing the demon fine manipulation even in this terrifying and inhuman form.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Typically the form of a Psychopomp, the Ophanim serve the God-Machine by overseeing and organizing infrastructure and human cults through their incredible intellect and their ability to see their servants and acquaintances no matter where they are. Their large and imposing presence ensures obedience in their servants and their bodies are very durable, to protect these essential planners. Demons with this form frequently use it to spy on friends and enemies, protecting themselves from would-be attackers through nearly divine terror and an impenetrable hide.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Modifications:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Armored Plates, Large Size, Inhuman Intelligence</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Technologies:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Glory and Terror, Clairvoyant Sight</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Propulsions:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Flight</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Processes:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Extra Mechanical Limbs</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Also, question! Activating a Partial Transformation into Demon Form takes 1 Aether and has a compromise roll. Do further uses of those abilities after they're activated incur more compromise rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T21:29:58-08:00","id":11053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1379-demonic-form-ideas\">Uhhhhmmmm\u2026</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T21:54:38-08:00","id":11061,"title":"","content":"Mea culpa, I forgot about that thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}